Hershey 'futural' single-stroke font

Created by Dr. Allen V. Hershey at the U.S. National Bureau of Standards (1967).
The Hershey fonts are in the public domain, with the traditional usage note from
the original distribution:

  This distribution of the Hershey Fonts may be used by anyone for any purpose,
  commercial or otherwise, freely and without restriction, providing that:
  1. The following acknowledgements must be distributed with the font data:
     - The Hershey Fonts were originally created by Dr. A. V. Hershey while
       working at the U. S. National Bureau of Standards.
     - The format of the Font data in this distribution was originally created by:
       James Hurt, Cognition, Inc.

Vendored into Curve Cut from the JHF data at
https://github.com/kamalmostafa/hershey-fonts (futural.jhf) via
tools/vendor_hershey.py, converted to the JSON stroke format in hershey-font.js.
